      "id": "F9",
      "statement": "What distinguishes the two alerts, which look alike as indicators (6 senders and 6 transfers each, within one hour): (a) totals of 357000 against 15000, with uniform 2500 credits for A-9895; (b) all six A-9278 credits are passed on through chains 3 links deep, against three of six A-9895 credits passed on 1 link deep; (c) the A-9278 onward route, three distinct accounts, was sent entirely from one device, D-568, while the A-9895 route shares no device. None of the downstream accounts A-5092, A-2897, A-4989 or A-1415 has its own fan-in alert. The A-9278 alert therefore comes with a recorded multi-hop, single-device onward structure. The A-9895 alert is a fan-in with a short, partial onward link and no device overlap.",
