  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "id": "H1",
      "statement": "Because one device, D-568, sent every hop from A-9278 through A-5092 and A-2897 to A-4989, with small amount reductions at each hop (138000 to 135000 to 132000; 210000 to 206000 to 202000), these accounts may be controlled by one party moving collected funds in layers. The data records only device use and transfers; it does not establish common control, ownership or fraud.",
      "references": [
        "S1",
        "R1",
        "E07",
        "E08",
        "E09",
        "E10",
        "E11",
        "E12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "H2",
      "statement": "The A-9895 alert, with uniform 2500 credits and only part of them passed on in a single hop, may be benign collection activity (for example, a shared bill or a group payment) rather than mule activity. That is an interpretation; the data does not establish the purpose.",
      "references": [
        "I2",
        "R2",
        "N1",
        "N2",
        "N3",
        "N4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "H3",
      "statement": "A-9278 forwarded 348000 of the 357000 it received. The 3000 to 4000 shortfall at each later hop could be fees or retained amounts. That is not recorded.",
